  "_membership_note": "assumable_by_admin / inherited_by_admin are read from pg_auth_members, and they are two different switches. Batch 002 confused `alter role r noinherit` (whether r inherits from roles it belongs to) with the grant's inherit_option (whether the grantee inherits from r), and left postgres holding these roles ambiently while its own comment said the opposite. Batch 003 corrected it. Both are asserted here because the record claiming one thing while the database did another is the defect, not the privilege itself."
